# Supply-chain age gate for the harness's own npm project: never resolve a
# dependency version published less than 7 days ago. The repo root's
# `npmMinimalAgeGate: 7d` is a YARN setting and does not cover this tree, which
# has its own package-lock.json.
#
# ⚠️ THIS FILE AND THE REPO-ROOT .npmrc ARE BOTH REQUIRED. They cover different
# npm modes, and neither one covers both (all four rows measured, 2026-08-04):
#
#   run from this directory                     | gate that applies
#   --------------------------------------------|---------------------------
#   npm install --package-lock-only             | ROOT .npmrc. npm treats the
#     (workspace-aware: npm walks up, finds     | monorepo as the project and
#      escher's root package.json)              | prints "ignoring workspace
#                                               | config" for THIS file.
#   npm install --package-lock-only \           | THIS file. The harness is its
#     --workspaces=false                        | own project, and the root
#                                               | .npmrc is NOT consulted.
#
# So do not delete this file because you saw npm warn that it is ignored — the
# warning is emitted only in the workspace-aware mode. In the standalone mode
# this file is the ONLY thing gating the resolve, and that mode matters twice:
#   1. it is the invocation that actually completes inside escher (the plain
#      workspace-aware one dies on `EUNSUPPORTEDPROTOCOL: workspace:^` from
#      sibling packages, and/or OOMs reconciling the whole monorepo — both
#      pre-existing, unrelated to this gate);
#   2. this directory ships to /home/user/.self in every agent sandbox, where
#      there is no parent workspace at all, so npm always reads this file when
#      an agent installs something for itself.
#
# `npm ci` is unaffected (it replays the lockfile without re-resolving), so the
# sandbox image build in anyone-sandbox-system/system/build-install.sh keeps
# working even when the lock pins a same-day version.
#
# OUR OWN PACKAGES (@skydiveai/*) are exempt from the gate in spirit — they
# publish from our own registry, so the public-scrutiny rationale doesn't
# apply. npm has no per-scope exclude, so pass the override explicitly with a
# pinned spec when bumping one of ours:
#   npm install @skydiveai/<pkg>@<version> --workspaces=false --min-release-age=0
#
# For anything NOT ours, override only when a same-day release is genuinely
# required (a CVE fix):
#   npm install --package-lock-only --workspaces=false --min-release-age=0
min-release-age=7
